'' A CALL CHECK SCORES AGAINST AN OVERLOAD SET AND CANNOT BIND IS NOT LOWERED AS THE FIRST
'' OVERLOAD. 'P4( t )' ties two conversion constructors -- LDay's, with a defaulted tail, and
'' LE's -- and fbc-modern 1.20 says error 98 (ambiguous; measured 2026-11-23). Check reports a
'' tie only over builtin and pointer arguments, so it said nothing, and lowering ran the name's
'' binding, the first overload declared: tiko printed 'P4 LDay 12'. Check now marks the call
'' (SemanticInfo.unbound, overload.tiko ResolveCall_) and every call-lowering path refuses a
'' marked one, so the build stops at the call. TKO0994 is the stop, not the goal: when the
'' tie report learns to trust UDT arguments this becomes TKO0660, fbc's 98.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -c tests/diagnostics/src/overload-unbound-refused.bas -o tests/diagnostics/src/overload-unbound-refused.o
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 4
'' EXPECT-OUT: overload-unbound-refused.bas(18,1): error TKO0994
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 1
